---
import '../styles/policy-visual.css';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---
<Base title="Website terms" description="Model information, image use, vehicle inquiries and order-specific written terms for KEEYAK Auto.">
 <Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'Website Terms'}]}/>
 <PageHero title="Website terms" subtitle="Model references and the written agreement for your purchase"/>
 <section class="policy-visual shell">
  <div class="policy-group policy-group--illustrated" data-core-module data-module="reference-scope"><div class="policy-group-copy"><h2>Using model information and company records</h2><p>This website provides passenger-car model references and purchasing information. A model page does not confirm stock, identify an individual used car, set a binding price or establish manufacturer authorization or destination eligibility.</p><p>Specifications describe the listed model or version. Model photographs do not confirm that a car is in stock. Some model images have edited backgrounds; these images do not document actual facilities, inspections or deliveries.</p></div><figure><img src="/images/catalog/toyota/camry/toyota-camry-front-three-quarter-left.webp" alt="Toyota Camry model reference photograph; availability and exact version need confirmation" width="1448" height="1086" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Model reference · exact version to confirm</figcaption></figure></div>
  <div class="policy-group" data-core-module data-module="inquiry-preparation"><h2>What a vehicle inquiry does</h2><p>Review inquiry prepares a draft. Send inquiry submits it to the website, which displays an inquiry reference only after saving it. Submitting the form does not reserve a car or create a purchase contract. The form does not take payment. Email and WhatsApp are separate contact channels; opening either app does not submit this website form.</p><p>Read how we handle drafts, submitted inquiries and website activity records in the <a class="text-link" href="/privacy/">privacy information</a>.</p></div>
  <div class="policy-group policy-group--illustrated" data-core-module data-module="written-order"><div class="policy-group-copy"><h2>Written offers and purchase agreements</h2><p>The agreed written offer and contract govern the purchase. Confirm the vehicle, condition, availability and quantity. Put pricing and timing in writing, along with the required documents and each party's responsibilities.</p><p>Agree payment stages and the terms for changes, cancellation and refunds in the contract. The inspection and shipping arrangements also need to be confirmed, as do warranty coverage and support. This website does not provide a general guarantee for these matters.</p><a class="button button-outline" href="/export-services/buying-guide/">Review the buying guide</a></div><figure class="policy-ui-reference policy-checklist-reference"><figcaption>Buying-guide screenshot · topics to agree, not an offer</figcaption><a href="/images/nest-site-20261019/ui/quotation-topics.png" aria-label="Open the topics to agree, not an offer screenshot"><img src="/images/nest-site-20261019/ui/quotation-topics.png" alt="Website checklist: vehicle price, currency, Incoterm and named place, included services and validity" width="576" height="828" loading="lazy"/></a></figure></div>
  <div class="policy-group" data-core-module data-module="destination-and-questions"><h2>Import requirements and commercial questions</h2><p>The buying guide helps you prepare questions for a purchase. It does not confirm import eligibility; check current requirements for the actual vehicle and destination. The agreement should name the parties responsible for export documents and local import formalities, including taxes and registration.</p><p>Contact <a class="text-link" href="mailto:contact@keeyak.com">contact@keeyak.com</a> to clarify a vehicle requirement or the proposed commercial terms.</p><a class="button button-outline" href="/contact/">Contact details</a></div>
 </section>
</Base>
